        <body>
            <div xml:id="d447">

                <pb facs="0612" n="506" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg506"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Sleeper to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-01-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 16, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1441.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise the department
                    that a presidential decree of general application, providing a sanitary
                    organization for the whole island and regulating in minute detail all matters
                    pertaining to sanitation, has been published in the “Official Gazette” of
                    January 12, 1906.</p>
                <pb facs="0613" n="507" xml:id="pg507"/>
                <p>This decree, which contains 30 chapters and 662 articles, is now being rendered
                    into English by the legation, and upon the completion of the translation will be
                    transmitted to the department.</p>
                <p>Opinion in official and business circles seems to indicate that considerable
                    opposition to the enforcement of the provisions of the decree will be
                    encountered among the business interests, business men declaring that it unduly
                    interferes with their individual independence in the arrangement of their own
                    affairs.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacob Sleeper</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
